      "writtenOn": "2022-01-07T08:53:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How is this different from the existing NetworkCapabilities#hasConnectivityManagedCapability? Could you adapt/rename/reuse that instead of adding this new method here?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 832,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 832,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "9dbf1d39407f337abf2ca4d3e1ea50467cdecc67",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41d07489_2e32b4a6",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkAgent.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 832,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-07T14:40:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This test is broader and enforcing. In followup patches, this method will gain domain-specific checks : if the capabilities have TRANSPORT_CELLULAR, accessUids must contain 0 or 1 UID and if 1 then it must be the carrier config package ; if it has NET_CAP_INTERNAL_NETWORK the device must have FEATURE_AUTO. Neither of these really fit in hasConnectivityManagedCapability.\n\nToday there is only one call to hasConnectivityManagedCapability and it\u0027s only used to check whether to emit a Log.wtf. I can incorporate that method into this one – it would probably be an improvement.\n\nHowever it would be a change of behavior observable by network factories.  I haven\u0027t heard from OEMs complaining about this, but since all hasConnectivityManagedCapability does is log a wtf, I think it\u0027s difficult to guarantee this would not break any existing use case.\n\nIn any case, if we\u0027re going to do this, it should be a separate patch.",
      "parentUuid": "8d2e04c0_11e3d265",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 832,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 832,
        "endChar": 63
