      "writtenOn": "2022-01-07T08:53:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The processCapabilitiesFromAgent call just a few lines below makes another copy. Can we avoid making two copies so soon after each other?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3315,
        "startChar": 68,
        "endLine": 3315,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "9dbf1d39407f337abf2ca4d3e1ea50467cdecc67",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a9800600_e4238619",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 3315,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-07T14:40:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not really. The copy here is meant to avoid mutating an object that belongs to another component, when it comes from a provider in the same process. The copy inside processCapabilitiesFromAgent is meant to keep a copy of the original object that was sent by the agent, which needs to be distinct both from the object actually sent by the agent (which the agent can mutate) and to the capabilities we\u0027ll keep in the agent (which CS can mutate). So we really need three objects.\n\nIn fact, the old code was mutating ownerUid on the object passed by the agent, which may really be an object that the agent holds a reference to.\n\nI did however change the patch in response to your comment : I moved restrictCapabilitiesFromNetworkAgent inside processCapabilitiesFromAgent, since that\u0027s where it morally belongs. That makes the patch a little bit more dangerous though, because I had to move the call to processCapabilitiesFromAgent in registerNetworkAgentInternal to handleRegisterNetworkAgent – since restrictCapabilitiesFromNetworkAgent will eventually have to run on the handler thread to see an up-to-date value for the carrier config package for the CBS feature.\nI don\u0027t think this is very dangerous as nobody is supposed to have a reference to the pending NAI, but it deserves some scrutiny.",
      "parentUuid": "df690fc8_4a8dd98e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3315,
        "startChar": 68,
        "endLine": 3315,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "9dbf1d39407f337abf2ca4d3e1ea50467cdecc67",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
